From 7e716e2755a4f58743be4e193cc1f97513839a47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateus Nascimento <mateus.soaresdonascimento@windriver.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:45:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix composite alarms with prometheus sub-rules

PrometheusRule.validate_alarm() stored the project scope on the
PrometheusRule class instead of on the rule being validated. Once an API
worker had created or updated a prometheus alarm, as_dict() of every
later PrometheusRule in that worker included scope_to_project. The
composite rule validation, which runs twice per request, then rejected
composite alarms with a prometheus sub-rule with "Unknown attribute for
argument data: scope_to_project".

Keep the scope on the rule, leave scope_to_project out of the WSME check
of composite sub-rules, and set it on the prometheus sub-rules of a
composite alarm the same way as for a prometheus alarm.

Add functional tests for composite alarms with prometheus sub-rules,
including one created after a prometheus alarm and one stored without
a scope and then updated.

Carried from the upstream review
https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/aodh/+/1007951 while it is still
under review. Drop this patch once a Debian Salsa aodh release contains
the fix.

Closes-Bug: #2168896
Change-Id: I85a9d66902f3486d65c30d525624c714df720c23
Signed-off-by: Mateus Nascimento <mateus.soaresdonascimento@windriver.com>
